From: n4-dispatch-residual <agent@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:41:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 161/257] perf(cpu): dedup AVX-512 per-launch artifact
 validation (n4-dispatch-residual)

launch() validates the primary AVX-512 artifact and then _decode_artifact()
validates it again; each fallback candidate re-validates the primary once
more.  On a 6728-op program that repeats CoreProgram.from_dict(),
canonical_json()+sha256 and the full lower_avx512() semantic comparison.

Add a per-launch _LaunchValidationMemo keyed by the immutable Artifact
identity (and its frozen metadata mapping).  The memo is created inside one
launch() call and dropped when it returns, so:

* every launch still rejects tampered metadata / version / digest mismatches;
* replacing artifact.metadata (identity change) forces full re-validation;
* a changed declared program_digest still misses the digest memo and is
  recomputed and rejected;
* fallback candidates reuse the primary result but are validated themselves.

The digest re-check keeps the fail-closed behaviour; no dispatch semantics,
Core IR/ABI contract or other backend is touched.  Focused tests pin the
memo, the tamper/version rejections and bit-identical repeated launches.
